Session: 2026-10-15 14:17 UTC
Plan: plan/2026/09/19-phase-18-compatibility-release-gate.md
Scope: P18-V01 Remoting connectTimeoutMillis Bootstrap timing slice

Source review
- Compared pinned Java NettyRemotingClient.start(), fetchBootstrap(), and
  createBootstrap() with Rust RemotingClient startup and connection selection.
- Java configures direct Bootstrap at start; proxy Bootstrap is created and
  cached on first use per CIDR, reading the then-current config value.
- Rust previously used only the start snapshot for direct and proxy dials, and
  NameServer scans imposed an extra deadline that did not match Bootstrap
  timeout behavior when the configured value was zero or changed for a proxy.

Implementation
- Code commit: aca955cd fix(remoting): match proxy bootstrap timeout timing.
- Rust now snapshots direct timeout at start, caches live timeout on first
  matched proxy-CIDR use, reuses that value for that CIDR, and reads newer
  values for later CIDRs. Reachability scans use an optional operation deadline
  so zero means no separate connect cap.
- Added Rust tests for post-start proxy timeout capture/cache, proxy scan
  timeout sampling, and zero-timeout NameServer scanning.
- Extended Java RemotingLiveConfigProbe to verify direct start-time capture,
  cached proxy reuse, and first-use capture for another CIDR.
- Updated the connectTimeoutMillis row in
  docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md and appended this revision's
  evidence to docs/release-checklist.md. No plan files were edited.

